1
00:01:42,519 --> 00:01:44,062
‎From what you've told me,

2
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:47,398
‎I can't rule out the possibility that
‎he's experiencing cyberpsychosis.

3
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:49,567
‎I need more information.

4
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:51,486
‎Can you describe
‎his behavior in more detail?

5
00:01:51,569 --> 00:01:55,073
‎What symptoms
‎should I keep an eye out for?

6
00:01:55,156 --> 00:01:59,077
‎Has he ever acted... not himself?
‎Even temporarily.

7
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:03,998
‎There was this one time
‎he got pretty weird...

8
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:07,377
‎Aha! Was he more... girlish?

9
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:10,380
‎Girlish? I dunno?

10
00:02:10,463 --> 00:02:12,924
‎Was actin' real strange, is all.

11
00:02:13,007 --> 00:02:15,885
‎And this only happened once?

12
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:16,970
‎I think...

13
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:21,015
‎Can cyberpsychosis flip
‎your whole personality?

14
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:23,184
‎Not necessarily, no.

15
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:25,603
‎How about hearing voices
‎that aren't there?

16
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:28,731
‎You mean like an imaginary friend?

17
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:31,276
‎Uh... I'm just spitballin'.

18
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:33,820
‎-Are you sure?
‎-Yeah.

19
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:35,530
‎Appreciate the info.

20
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:37,824
‎Can I ping ya back
‎if I notice anything else?

21
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:39,117
‎Of course.

22
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,119
‎Thanks... Talk to ya later.

23
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:48,251
‎So Capri hasn't overwritten her host...
‎but they talk to each other?

24
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:51,004
‎Maybe the overwrite is still in progress.

25
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:55,508
‎Which would mean... Agh, I don't know!

26
00:02:57,218 --> 00:02:59,637
‎There's too many unknown variables.

27
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:02,640
‎Why'd you run away? Capri...

28
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,143
‎Initiate test.

29
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:23,411
‎Capri, enough. Stop clownin' around.

30
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:25,955
‎Honestly...

31
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,165
‎Most impressive.

32
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:32,211
‎She can hack or destroy
‎any electronic system in an instant.

33
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:36,424
‎This will revolutionize
‎how we conduct warfare.

34
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:39,052
‎Well, there are still a few bugs.

35
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:44,015
‎Ah, shit. Yank the chip.

36
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:45,767
‎-On it.
‎-What just happened?

37
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:51,022
‎On average, only about 7% of test subjects
‎survive Capricorn's installation.

38
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:57,028
‎About half die within 12 hours.
‎And none have ever lived beyond the 48.

39
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:59,948
‎That's completely unsustainable.

40
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:01,908
‎It boils down to compatibility.

41
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:03,451
‎We'll find a compatible host,

42
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:05,745
‎and that will help us
‎in finding a permanent solution.

43
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:09,499
‎This thing, this fusion
‎of digital constructs...

44
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:11,251
‎What if it escapes into cyberspace?

45
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:14,963
‎Precisely why it requires
‎a human host in the first place.

46
00:04:15,046 --> 00:04:19,384
‎The fragility of organic matter
‎serves as the perfect safeguard.

47
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:22,637
‎Worst case, we can implant the host body

48
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,973
‎with explosives
‎or toxins as a kill switch.

49
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:31,980
‎This way, we also eliminate the threat
‎of her escaping across the Blackwall.

50
00:04:33,564 --> 00:04:36,276
‎So the body serves as her prison.

51
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:43,324
‎-Next test subject.
‎-Yes, ma'am.

52
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:48,079
‎Since Tanaka's death,
‎it's like Counterintel's gone dark.

53
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,873
‎Our patience is wearing thin.

54
00:04:51,416 --> 00:04:53,209
‎How many subjects dead?

55
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:55,586
‎We'll never find a host.

56
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:57,880
‎Additional funding is out of the question.

57
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:02,885
‎It's all right, Capri.

58
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,972
‎Ma'am, this is going too far!

59
00:05:06,055 --> 00:05:07,890
‎They won't take you away from me.

60
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,396
‎No! Stop the test!

61
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:23,156
‎Return fire! Power weapons only!

62
00:05:23,239 --> 00:05:25,533
‎-Fuck! Agh! My face!
‎-Smart guns won't work!

63
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:28,745
‎This was a waste of time.
‎A disappointment.

64
00:05:29,370 --> 00:05:31,247
‎But Capri is almost complete!

65
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:33,666
‎She's perfect!
‎Just missing the right host!

66
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:35,793
‎It's over.

67
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:39,172
‎Project Capricorn is hereby terminated.

68
00:05:39,255 --> 00:05:41,883
‎Capri? Don't you fuckin' touch her!

69
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:46,471
‎Capri!

70
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:50,683
‎Morning already.

71
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:53,644
‎You oughta scamper on back.

72
00:05:58,274 --> 00:06:00,401
‎Really am the only one who can see you.

73
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:04,155
‎I ain't a hallucination!
‎How many times do I gotta explain it!

74
00:06:04,238 --> 00:06:06,949
‎Yeah, yeah, digital construct, I get it...

75
00:06:07,533 --> 00:06:09,702
‎Just stop eavesdroppin'
‎on my thoughts, will ya?

76
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:12,705
‎Pretty big ask considerin'
‎we share the same brain.

77
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:14,415
‎Whatever...

78
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:19,629
‎You haven't even thanked me for fixin'
‎your brain and gettin' ya on your feet.

79
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:21,339
‎Saved your life, don't ya know!

80
00:06:21,422 --> 00:06:24,550
‎So? My body's the only thing
‎keepin' you alive, too.

81
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:27,762
‎Details! What's wrong
‎with a lil give-and-take?

82
00:06:28,346 --> 00:06:30,473
‎Fact is... you did get me outta that bed.

83
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:33,476
‎Got me past hospital security.

84
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:36,354
‎I believe you... I guess.

85
00:06:37,855 --> 00:06:39,232
‎Sheesh, you're so weird.

86
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:43,402
‎-Weird?
‎-Your body's failing on every level.

87
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:46,072
‎Thought you'd be all,
‎"Yay, I can walk again!"

88
00:06:46,155 --> 00:06:47,657
‎You're almost all healthy now!

89
00:06:48,157 --> 00:06:49,242
‎I ‎am‎ happy...

90
00:06:50,326 --> 00:06:52,578
‎But... it's not enough.

91
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:54,747
‎Listen, I can't make you fly
‎or anything like that.

92
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:57,250
‎So don't go gettin' greedy.

93
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:00,628
‎At least... not unless we get
‎the chip back, right?

94
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:04,632
‎Yup. Half my programming
‎is still lodged inside him.

95
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:08,261
‎And if I have all of you,
‎you can fix me completely?

96
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:10,555
‎Oh no, way beyond that.

97
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:13,391
‎Beyond that? Can't even imagine it.

98
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:14,517
‎Yeah?

99
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:19,397
‎Because that was...
‎the best my body could ever do.

100
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:24,569
‎I can take you back
‎to how you were. Promise!

101
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:41,252
‎You're still Capri, right?

102
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:43,629
‎Right?

103
00:07:45,506 --> 00:07:46,507
‎Capri...

104
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,477
‎Oh, are we rolling?

105
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:00,271
‎Hey NC, we're comin' to ya live today!

106
00:08:00,354 --> 00:08:02,773
‎Let's go! Kick it off, D!

107
00:08:03,441 --> 00:08:06,527
‎To the butchers responsible
‎for torching my clan.

108
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:10,281
‎I've been tellin' you to step up,
‎but you've given me nothing.

109
00:08:10,364 --> 00:08:13,201
‎The next target shows how serious I am.

110
00:08:13,284 --> 00:08:14,785
‎Jake Collins.

111
00:08:14,869 --> 00:08:17,413
‎Deputy Chief
‎of Arasaka Counterintelligence.

112
00:08:17,497 --> 00:08:19,290
‎He's gettin' hit as I speak.

113
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:26,255
‎Yo! He ran off that way!

114
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:29,550
‎Hey! Come on out!

115
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:30,885
‎Got one!

116
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:35,932
‎Roman, that's a killer angle!
‎Helluva money shot!

117
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:43,689
‎My arm...

118
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:45,441
‎Someone find it...

119
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:46,901
‎-Someone find my arm...
‎-Yo.

120
00:08:46,984 --> 00:08:49,987
‎Ah! I don't know anything... Nothing!

121
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:53,449
‎Bullshit. Why would Counterintel
‎be kept out of the loop?

122
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,201
‎I'm telling the truth!

123
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:57,161
‎Nothing about a nomad camp--

124
00:08:57,745 --> 00:09:01,707
‎Then give me some names!
‎Who the fuck knows? Tell me!

125
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:05,336
‎I don't know any names.
‎They just transferred here recently!

126
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:08,673
‎I don't know anything.
‎Please... I need help.

127
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:10,508
‎Please...

128
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:14,178
‎-Let's delta. D! Gotta go!
‎-What?

129
00:09:20,142 --> 00:09:22,103
‎-My arm...
‎-Last call for loot!

130
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:24,438
‎What? Already?

131
00:09:33,614 --> 00:09:36,784
‎Man, D's a machine.
‎Could wipe 'Saka by hisself.

132
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:41,455
‎Right! Like, what's stoppin' us
‎from hittin' 'em dead on!

133
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:47,461
‎Don't throw your shit, choomie.

134
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:48,754
‎Mega rude.

135
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:52,466
‎How have I not learned
‎a single goddamn thing? Fuck!

136
00:10:18,826 --> 00:10:21,996
‎-Huh? Who's this bitch?
‎-What do I do?

137
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:23,914
‎Run her over.

138
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:25,875
‎No. She's a friend.

139
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:30,046
‎-How'd she find us?
‎-I pinged her.

140
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:33,507
‎Did you watch?

141
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:36,218
‎-I did.
‎-And?

142
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:39,513
‎This mean you're ready to join the fight?
‎Is that why you're here, Omi?

143
00:10:40,264 --> 00:10:43,017
‎What you're doing is completely unhinged.

144
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:44,393
‎So you liked it?

145
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:45,936
‎Is that what you think?

146
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:47,813
‎It scared me.

147
00:10:47,897 --> 00:10:50,941
‎It's not like you don't know
‎where this road leads, right?

148
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:53,319
‎Course I do. Doesn't matter.

149
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:57,156
‎What you're doing now...
‎it's the same shit those corpos did to us.

150
00:10:58,240 --> 00:10:59,575
‎The same?

151
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:02,953
‎This senseless violence... it isn't you.

152
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:04,288
‎Not the old you.

153
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:07,583
‎Is there even a point to all this?

154
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:09,627
‎You know what it is.

155
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,796
‎-Revenge?
‎-Yeah.

156
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:15,841
‎It's insanity. You've gone too far.
‎Innocent folks are gettin' caught in it!

157
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,843
‎They're all 'Saka!

158
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:19,887
‎I'm just tryna smoke out
‎the ones still hiding!

159
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:23,349
‎So what, you're gonna flatline everyone
‎at Arasaka just because?

160
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:25,601
‎Why the fuck did you even come here?

161
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:27,853
‎To rag on me? Go home!

162
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:30,231
‎No! I came to stop you!

163
00:11:32,316 --> 00:11:34,068
‎The fuck?

164
00:11:34,151 --> 00:11:36,821
‎What the hell are you doin'?

165
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:39,198
‎Giving you a taste of your own medicine!

166
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:45,162
‎Damn it!

167
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:56,882
‎Fuck you, Omi.

168
00:11:57,508 --> 00:12:01,762
‎What the hell am I supposed to do? Huh?

169
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:05,141
‎The fuck do I do?

170
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:07,393
‎Tell me!

171
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:09,979
‎Stop it, D! You gotta chill!

172
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:11,772
‎-Outta the way, Roman.
‎-I'm not movin'!

173
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,858
‎-You--
‎-Your gonk revenge plan's not working!

174
00:12:13,941 --> 00:12:15,401
‎Time to give it up!

175
00:12:15,484 --> 00:12:17,153
‎Where'd that come from?

176
00:12:17,236 --> 00:12:21,282
‎She's right. Haven't been yourself.
‎The D I know--

177
00:12:21,365 --> 00:12:22,533
‎Just shut up!

178
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:25,035
‎The D you know? Fuck you.

179
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:26,537
‎You two don't know shit!

180
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:36,547
‎Fuck!

181
00:12:46,557 --> 00:12:47,558
‎Um...

182
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:50,811
‎So you were in the same clan as D?

183
00:12:54,523 --> 00:12:55,774
‎And you are?

184
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:59,528
‎Can't say I approve.

185
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:04,533
‎That is, a kid your age
‎taggin' along with him.

186
00:13:04,617 --> 00:13:06,452
‎It doesn't sit well with me at all.

187
00:13:07,244 --> 00:13:09,288
‎Why not walk away?

188
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:12,458
‎You seem fed up
‎with how he's been acting.

189
00:13:13,834 --> 00:13:17,963
‎-I saw him laughing a little while ago.
‎-Laughing?

190
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:20,883
‎The first time D tapped into that power...

191
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:24,261
‎He just looked so happy.
‎Was like he couldn't stop laughin'.

192
00:13:25,429 --> 00:13:27,973
‎Like everything changed.
‎He seemed so different.

193
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:30,684
‎And I thought...

194
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:34,104
‎"Oh, so ‎that's‎ how this guy laughs."

195
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:36,357
‎Made me wonder if that was the real D.

196
00:13:36,982 --> 00:13:41,737
‎Made me wanna catch
‎that side of D on film again.

197
00:13:44,114 --> 00:13:45,115
‎Yeah. I understand.

198
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:48,285
‎He... He's got a really good smile.

199
00:13:48,869 --> 00:13:50,246
‎Here's your order.

200
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,874
‎So, you haven't seen him in a while?

201
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:56,502
‎No. Not since you know what.

202
00:13:57,294 --> 00:14:01,006
‎Um... Can I ask what happened?

203
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:06,303
‎First, you mind turnin' that thing off?
‎I don't much like being on camera.

204
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:08,264
‎Sorry. Habit.

205
00:14:09,139 --> 00:14:10,766
‎So what has he told you?

206
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:12,601
‎Bits and pieces...

207
00:14:12,685 --> 00:14:15,771
‎-Never goes into detail.
‎-Yeah.

208
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:20,276
‎He was all smiles on that day, too.

209
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:24,280
‎We stole some random jalopy from a motel.

210
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:27,658
‎On the way home,
‎he was cacklin' like a coyote.

211
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:30,494
‎Being his usual goofy self.

212
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:35,541
‎He was still laughin'
‎when we saw the smoke.

213
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:40,170
‎In the desert,
‎you can see smoke from miles out.

214
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:43,924
‎We could tell it was comin' from camp.

215
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:48,053
‎We weren't laughin' anymore.
‎We went real quiet, then.

216
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:53,559
‎The rest is kind of a blur.
‎That was the last time I saw him.

217
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:58,564
‎Not once did the fool ever contact me.
‎For all I knew, he was buzzard bait.

218
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:01,692
‎I had my own troubles to deal with, so...

219
00:15:02,192 --> 00:15:04,820
‎-Um... Not sure I should ask.
‎-Ask what?

220
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:07,072
‎Were you guys like... romantic?

221
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:15,289
‎Was that your takeaway back there?
‎A spat between lovebirds?

222
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:19,460
‎Well, uh... they say love comes
‎in all shapes and sizes...

223
00:15:21,962 --> 00:15:25,424
‎That's too good!
‎Now I see why David likes you.

224
00:15:25,507 --> 00:15:27,134
‎Huh? David?

225
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:29,386
‎What, he never told you his name?

226
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:32,765
‎Oh, that's right,
‎goes by D these days, doesn't he?

227
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:36,477
‎Gonna start calling him
‎by his first name now?

228
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,395
‎I could, but...

229
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:43,150
‎No. Only ever known him as D.
‎That's who he is.

230
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:44,777
‎Sure.

231
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:10,803
‎Avida? If you're looking
‎for Kiril, he's out right now.

232
00:16:11,303 --> 00:16:13,889
‎Just here to drop somethin' off
‎for him anyway.

233
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,980
‎Just slot this shard into his terminal.

234
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:22,815
‎It'll pull the files
‎we need automatically.

235
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:27,778
‎Got it from one of my old contacts.
‎Should still work.

236
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:32,616
‎Got it!

237
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:36,453
‎Avida?

238
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:38,455
‎What brings you here?

239
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:42,960
‎I came to see you...
‎They let me wait inside.

240
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:45,546
‎You could've called first.

241
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:47,965
‎What was so urgent?

242
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:51,051
‎Are you familiar with Soulkiller?

243
00:16:51,635 --> 00:16:56,265
‎Soulkiller? Of course I'm familiar.
‎But where is this coming from?

244
00:16:56,348 --> 00:17:00,060
‎Well, I thought that technology
‎could maybe save Talia.

245
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:02,646
‎If her body's failing,
‎why not find her a new one?

246
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:03,731
‎Impossible.

247
00:17:04,356 --> 00:17:06,400
‎Even if we managed
‎to create her construct,

248
00:17:06,483 --> 00:17:08,861
‎body transferal technology doesn't exist.

249
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:10,571
‎But there's potential!

250
00:17:10,654 --> 00:17:12,031
‎No, there isn't.

251
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:16,660
‎Besides which, Soulkiller
‎was proprietary to Arasaka.

252
00:17:16,744 --> 00:17:18,495
‎It's not a program they'll let anyone use.

253
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:21,498
‎But... doesn't Kang Tao
‎have its own version?

254
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:23,876
‎Where did you hear that?

255
00:17:23,959 --> 00:17:27,421
‎I didn't, just assumed.
‎And that sounded like a "yes."

256
00:17:27,504 --> 00:17:28,839
‎No, we don't.

257
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:30,049
‎Are you sure?

258
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:31,759
‎It's impossible.

259
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:34,219
‎Arasaka already cut
‎their commercial investment for it.

260
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:37,139
‎-Really?
‎-Yes.

261
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,600
‎You came all this way to ask that?

262
00:17:39,683 --> 00:17:41,351
‎So what if I did?

263
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:44,104
‎If this could save Talia's life,
‎shouldn't I?

264
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:45,189
‎You need to stay calm.

265
00:17:46,023 --> 00:17:49,526
‎You're starting to sound like Talia
‎with this cyber-fetishization talk.

266
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:52,905
‎Miracle cures, pseudoscience,
‎these things won't help.

267
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:55,532
‎We must remain grounded.

268
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,534
‎You mean, like you?

269
00:17:57,618 --> 00:17:58,952
‎That's right.

270
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:01,330
‎No... You're right.

271
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:05,250
‎Shouldn't have barged in on you like this.

272
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:07,669
‎I know you've been under
‎a lot of pressure.

273
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:11,048
‎-Go on home, get some rest.
‎-Yeah.

274
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:16,553
‎Avida?

275
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:21,016
‎You're not the only one
‎who wants to help Talia.

276
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:23,560
‎I hope you understand that.

277
00:18:25,729 --> 00:18:26,730
‎I do.

278
00:19:02,432 --> 00:19:03,851
‎Talia?

279
00:19:20,951 --> 00:19:22,119
‎Nova!

280
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:36,800
‎Soooo preem!

281
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:39,136
‎Can't believe the projector still works!

282
00:19:39,219 --> 00:19:40,220
‎You like it?

283
00:19:40,304 --> 00:19:43,599
‎Course I do!
‎Always dreamed of watchin' a movie here!

284
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:44,892
‎Thought so.

285
00:19:44,975 --> 00:19:46,810
‎Too bad this movie's a total stinker.

286
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,896
‎Bushido X‎ is showin' too.

287
00:19:49,396 --> 00:19:50,856
‎Nah, this one's fine.

288
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:53,859
‎Ah, before I forget.

289
00:19:53,942 --> 00:19:55,485
‎Take your pick.

290
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:59,198
‎You have two cams?
‎I call dibs on the little one.

291
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:04,286
‎-Ooh, it's working!
‎-Hey, listen...

292
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:06,246
‎What? Oh, the hospital?

293
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:07,998
‎I snuck out!

294
00:20:11,335 --> 00:20:13,712
‎Come on...

295
00:20:13,795 --> 00:20:16,006
‎Aw, were you worried for me?

296
00:20:16,089 --> 00:20:17,758
‎Course I was!

297
00:20:17,841 --> 00:20:21,720
‎Glad you're doin' okay, but come on...

298
00:20:22,846 --> 00:20:26,892
‎Won't lie, it wasn't great.
‎Couldn't walk 'til the other day.

299
00:20:27,976 --> 00:20:29,645
‎Right? Can you believe it?

300
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:36,652
‎Sis, your survival stats are insane.
‎For real, for real.

301
00:20:37,527 --> 00:20:42,199
‎Teach me! I wanna be a strong,
‎independent woman like you!

302
00:20:42,741 --> 00:20:44,701
‎What was that, you weirdo!

303
00:20:49,456 --> 00:20:52,584
‎Hey! Been meanin'
‎to apologize to you, Talia!

304
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:53,669
‎To me?

305
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:55,963
‎You wound up in the hospital

306
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:58,966
‎-'‎cause of D's chip, right?
‎-‎Ah...

307
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:00,884
‎I'm really, really sorry.

308
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:03,095
‎Why are you apologizing?

309
00:21:03,178 --> 00:21:05,055
‎It's not like you did it.

310
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:06,932
‎I know, but... still...

311
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:10,435
‎To tell ya the truth,
‎wasn't doin' so hot anyway.

312
00:21:10,519 --> 00:21:13,480
‎Kinda worked out in the end, huh?

313
00:21:13,563 --> 00:21:14,690
‎What?

314
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:20,320
‎If we're gettin' things off our chest,
‎suppose I should apologize to you too.

315
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:21,446
‎To me?

316
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:25,450
‎'Cause of me you had
‎to put up with that old geezer.

317
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:28,912
‎Always are gettin' me
‎in trouble. Even today.

318
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:32,457
‎You're a good guy, Roman.

319
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:34,960
‎I dunno 'bout that...

320
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:39,965
‎Bastard thought he was so funny,
‎tellin' me I don't know love.

321
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:44,136
‎What a jerk.
‎Can't he tell I'm too sick to date?

322
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:46,263
‎Just stop to think for two millisecs.

323
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:50,100
‎-Yeah... Didn't seem like he bought it.
‎-What's that?

324
00:21:50,183 --> 00:21:54,563
‎That I could be your boyfriend.
‎Idea of it had him crackin' up.

325
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:56,898
‎Dunno why. I like you.

326
00:21:58,650 --> 00:22:00,652
‎Your film.

327
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:02,487
‎Oh...

328
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:05,365
‎But you like me, don't you?

329
00:22:06,908 --> 00:22:08,118
‎Uh... I mean...

330
00:22:09,619 --> 00:22:10,704
‎Don't you?

331
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:15,751
‎Even if you don't,
‎still hope you're willin' to help me.

332
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:17,210
‎Well, 'course...

333
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:20,672
‎Can you take me to D?

334
00:22:21,214 --> 00:22:22,716
‎Why the heck would you want that?

335
00:22:22,799 --> 00:22:23,884
‎Can't help?

336
00:22:23,967 --> 00:22:25,761
‎I can, but...

337
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:28,722
‎But what? Those vids all over the city...

338
00:22:29,389 --> 00:22:30,432
‎That's him, isn't it?

339
00:22:31,183 --> 00:22:33,769
‎And you're his cameraman? Right?

340
00:22:33,852 --> 00:22:35,479
‎Yeah, but...

341
00:22:35,562 --> 00:22:38,190
‎There some reason we shouldn't meet?

342
00:22:38,273 --> 00:22:39,524
‎Why would you want to?

343
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:42,986
‎I mean, was 'cause of him
‎you landed in the hospital!

344
00:22:43,862 --> 00:22:44,988
‎That's...

345
00:22:47,699 --> 00:22:48,742
‎Why?

346
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:52,370
‎-Talia?
‎-Sorry, gotta bounce.

347
00:22:52,454 --> 00:22:54,331
‎Wha... now? What about D?

348
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:58,251
‎Let's hit pause. I'll buzz ya back.

349
00:22:58,335 --> 00:23:00,045
‎Gotta meet up with a choom.

350
00:23:01,797 --> 00:23:04,007
‎Your cam. Can I borrow it?

351
00:23:04,091 --> 00:23:05,383
‎Uh, sure, yeah.

352
00:23:06,343 --> 00:23:07,636
‎See ya 'round.

353
00:23:13,225 --> 00:23:15,727
‎Why'd you stop me? What about the chip?

354
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:19,147
‎That lil cupcake would go
‎to hell and back for you, you know.

355
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:22,275
‎Might even yank the chip out for you.

356
00:23:22,359 --> 00:23:24,569
‎Then lemme lay out the situation for him--

357
00:23:24,653 --> 00:23:26,780
‎You think that baby
‎would walk away unharmed?

358
00:23:28,657 --> 00:23:29,991
‎And think of the chip.

359
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:32,828
‎If it winds up lost or falls
‎in someone else's pocket,

360
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:35,205
‎our plan gets flushed down the crapper.

361
00:23:35,288 --> 00:23:37,165
‎Like if some corpo gets hold of it

362
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:39,292
‎-and cracks it open?
‎-Ding-ding!

363
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:43,922
‎Depending on what they find, there's
‎no telling what happens to either of us.

364
00:23:44,005 --> 00:23:46,675
‎It's not the safest option...

365
00:23:46,758 --> 00:23:51,429
‎but the fact that D has the chip
‎is a major opportunity.

366
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:53,974
‎We need to play this carefully.

367
00:23:54,057 --> 00:23:56,434
‎He has a bad habit of rushing into things.

368
00:23:57,602 --> 00:24:01,690
‎Still can't believe Kang Tao
‎has a Soulkiller all its own.

369
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:05,819
‎Got it through a backdoor deal
‎within Arasaka.

370
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:08,446
‎Almost no one knows.

371
00:24:09,614 --> 00:24:11,491
‎Doesn't matter. Take a look here.

372
00:24:14,953 --> 00:24:15,954
‎What are they?

373
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:18,081
‎Cryopreserved bodies, all of 'em.

374
00:24:18,665 --> 00:24:22,335
‎Stockpiled as would-be hosts
‎for minds extracted by Soulkiller.

375
00:24:22,419 --> 00:24:24,462
‎-Then...
‎-That's right.

376
00:24:24,546 --> 00:24:26,339
‎Kang Tao has all the tools we need.

377
00:24:26,423 --> 00:24:29,551
‎It's just the process itself
‎of mergin' mind with body

378
00:24:29,634 --> 00:24:31,386
‎that's still experimental.

379
00:24:31,469 --> 00:24:33,638
‎Avida, really sure about this?

380
00:24:33,722 --> 00:24:35,640
‎Practically an act of war
‎against your husband.

381
00:24:36,183 --> 00:24:39,102
‎I know. I've made my choice.

382
00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:43,148
‎You'll have to leave, flee the city,
‎unless you back outta this now.

383
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:45,609
‎A little late for that.

384
00:24:46,484 --> 00:24:48,528
‎Besides, we're runnin' outta time.

385
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:51,865
‎Soulkiller's bein' relocated
‎to a new facility. It's now or never.

386
00:24:53,909 --> 00:24:56,328
‎We can't take Talia in her condition...

387
00:24:56,411 --> 00:24:58,371
‎We'll do it ourselves.

388
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:02,792
‎Copy Soulkiller. Grab a body for her.

389
00:25:05,045 --> 00:25:06,463
‎You're right.

390
00:25:08,882 --> 00:25:10,133
‎Let's run it.

391
00:26:49,941 --> 00:26:54,946
‎Subtitle translation by:
‎CD PROJEKT RED & Megumi Hunter
